# ROADMAP-NS — Heading locks for a ROADMAP rewrite

File: openOODA/audit/roadmap_ns_docs.oot
Survey only. Do not rewrite ROADMAP.oot in this pass. C emit + gcc remains product.

A ROADMAP rewrite is false if START.oot or SHIPPED.oot still name
section numbers or leftover jobs that the new outline drops.
Keep those numbers. Keep the 5.3 and 5.4 leftover blocks as they stand.

## 1. FORMAT and status words

FORMAT.oot status words (use these, and only these, on boards):
  done — works, verified with proof
  smoke — small verification check passes
  partial — part is implemented
  residual — wanted, planned, not built
  open — in progress in the active sprint

ROADMAP.oot also names:
  stale — old leftover words; a later proof closed them

Do not invent other status words. Do not mark a leftover `done`
without proof. Do not reopen a checked OPEN-1..92 row unless its
proof is gone.

Every `.oot` file: header block, numbered headings, ASD-STE100,
strictly <= 256 lines.

## 2. START.oot heading locks

Board catalog (START §1 item 5):
