## 5. open52 required strings

`../ooda/scripts/open52_stale_smoke.oo` fails closed unless:

Live numbers on ROADMAP (outside any closed window):
  `RAM-cold` then `164s` within 80 characters (`grep -E`)
  exact `179 modules`

Closed-log heading must match this awk window:
  a `##` or `###` line that contains `Closed stale-word`
  OR `do not reopen`
  Tokens below that heading are allowed until the next `##` line.
  A later `###` line does not close the window.

Forbidden present-tense tokens outside that window,
and on all eight other boards (never allowed there):
  `523s`
  `174 modules`
  `No live registry`
  `AES still exits`
  `Clang link of full oodac is next`

SHIPPED must not contain `523s` at all.

Prints: C emit plus gcc remains product.

## 6. Keep numbers. Do not retitle START/SHIPPED.

DOCS recommend: keep ROADMAP section numbers.
Do not retitle START/SHIPPED to a new outline.

Reason: SHIPPED has many hard `§5.1` / `§5.3` / `§5.4` / `§6`
pointers. START names section 5 as this-cycle Open and names
section 6 as later. open52 locks the closed-log heading words,
not a section digit. The cheap honest path is: keep 5 / 5.1 /
5.3 / 5.4 / 6, keep 5.3 and 5.4 text, keep the §6 heading
words `Closed stale-word` and `do not reopen`.

After the rewrite, fix START (and RULES if you touch it) so
"section 6 residual tracks" is not a lie. Residual stay-facts
are §5.1. Section 6 is the closed log. Do not pick a §6 row.
That is a board-word fix, not a new product OPEN row.

